  "text": "Recipe: Cauliflower Potato Waffles\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Waffles\nIngredients: riced cauliflower, grated potatoes, onion, mint, cilantro, green chillies, Chaat Masala, ground flaxseed, turmeric powder, red chili powder, Salt\nCooking methods: microwave, cook, air-fry\nInstructions: BATTER: If using frozen grated potatoes and frozen riced cauliflower, microwave them for 5 minutes. Add all the ingredients and mix with hands to form a batter (make sure potatoes & cauliflower are not too hot).\nWAFFLES: Preheat the waffle maker as per instructions. Place a big lemon size ball of the mixture on waffle maker. Spread with a flat spoon and cook for 3-4 minutes.\nSERVE: Carefully remove waffles and serve them with sugar-free homemade tomato sauce or your favorite homemade chutneys & dressings.\nNotes: TIP: For crispiness, we may air fry cooked waffles for 3-4 minutes.",
